Steps to configure Authenticator App

 1. Download the Authenticator app from either the Apple App Store or the Android Google Play store. It's free. (We recommend using either the Google Authenticator app or the Microsoft Authenticator app)
 2. In Google Authenticator App: 
        At the bottom of your screen, two options will show up, "Scan barcode" and "Manual entry". You only need to choose one of these options to complete the process. Using the "Scan barcode" option scan the below QR Code or can use code: {{secretcode}}
    In Microsoft Authenticator App: 
        On the top right click on the menu icon > Add Account > other Account. And scan the below QR Code or can enter the code: {{secretcode}} manually

    {{secretcodeimg}}

 3. At this point, your 2-factor authentication has been configured and the app has been set up properly. Next, you may be required to enter the 6-digit code displayed on the authenticator app every time you log in.

